    fix(commands/bookmarks, commands/finder): user-authorized bookmark provenance for reveal/open (P0 Delta escalation)
    
    Why:
      Codex re-reviewed the P1-Delta `validate_user_path` lexical gate and
      escalated G3-E3 from P1 to P0. The contract in
      `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §4 states every path access must
      come from a user drop/open panel or authorized bookmark; the lexical
      gate alone only narrows the attack surface (any path under `/Users/`,
      `/Applications/`, `/Volumes/`, `/tmp/` was still admitted). P1-Delta
      weakened the contract to match the implementation; this commit raises
      the implementation to match the contract.
    
    What:
      New `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/bookmarks.rs`:
      - `BookmarkRegistry: Mutex<HashSet<PathBuf>>` Tauri-managed state
        keyed by the canonical path produced by `validate_user_path`.
      - `register_path_bookmark` / `clear_path_bookmark` IPC commands
        scoped to the same allow-list as `reveal_in_finder` / `open_path`.
      - `is_path_bookmarked(state, canonical) -> bool` Rust-internal helper.
      - 5 cargo unit tests: allow-list admit/reject, register-lookup-clear
        round-trip, idempotent clear, validator-rejects-before-registry.
    
      `commands/finder.rs`:
      - `validate_user_path` promoted to `pub(crate)` for bookmark module
        re-use; `FINDER_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` exposed `pub(crate)` for symmetry.
      - New `ensure_path_authorized` helper layers the registry lookup on
        top of the lexical gate; unbookmarked paths → `E3004 sync
        capability denied — no user-authorized bookmark`.
      - `reveal_in_finder` / `open_path` now take `tauri::State<'_,
        BookmarkRegistry>` and call `ensure_path_authorized` before the
        `open` / `open -R` shell-out.
      - 2 new cargo unit tests via the shared helper:
        `reveal_rejects_unbookmarked_path`, `reveal_allows_bookmarked_path`.
    
      `commands/mod.rs` and `lib.rs`:
      - Register the new module, manage `BookmarkRegistry::default()`, and
        add the two new commands to `invoke_handler`.
    
      `packages/plugin-organizer/src/finderClient.ts`:
      - Exposes `registerBookmark(path)` / `clearBookmark(path)` over the
        existing `useTauriInvoke` seam (red-line #4 preserved — no direct
        `@tauri-apps/api` import).
      - New `finderClient.test.ts` with 4 vitest cases covering all 4
        methods' `invoke(...)` shape.
    
      `packages/plugin-organizer/src/hooks/useFileDrop.ts`:
      - Optional `finderClient?: FinderClient` in `UseFileDropOptions`.
      - When provided, every dropped path is registered via
        `registerBookmark` (fire-and-forget with per-path warn-on-fail).
      - When absent, a one-shot console warning explains why subsequent
        reveal/open will be rejected with `E3004`. Keeps existing unit
        tests working without modification.
      - TODO row added for the user-initiated `Open…` panel path.
    
    Scope:
      - `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/bookmarks.rs` (new)
      - `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/finder.rs`
      - `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/mod.rs`
      - `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs`
      - `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/AUDIT.md`
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/src/finderClient.ts`
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/src/finderClient.test.ts` (new)
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/src/hooks/useFileDrop.ts`
      - `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md`
      - `docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/g3-organizer-batch/PROCESS-NOTE.md`
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/docs/dev_log.md`
    
    Risk:
      - Storage is in-memory only — every desktop restart clears the
        registry. Users must re-authorize a path (re-drop or re-open) after
        a restart before reveal/open work for it. This is intentionally
        more restrictive than the contract requires; every authorized path
        now has recent, explicit user provenance. A persistent
        security-scoped bookmark store remains a separate follow-up for
        the MAS sandbox build.
      - `useFileDrop` keeps its `finderClient` optional so the change does
        not propagate into the do-not-touch `OrganizerLayer` / test files;
        however, this means a misconfigured caller silently degrades to
        "every reveal/open returns E3004". The one-shot warn-on-missing
        keeps the failure mode visible in DevTools without surfacing it as
        a runtime exception.
    
    Docs:
      - `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §4 restored the strict "user
        drop/open panel or authorized bookmark" sentence, added rows for
        the two new commands, updated the reveal/open row to reference the
        `BookmarkRegistry`, and DELETED the previous "deferred bookmark
        enforcement" caveat. §7 G2.5 invariants table extended with a row
        for the new commands.
      - `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/AUDIT.md` adds the new
        commands and notes the registry lookup on the finder row.
      - `docs/workflow/roadmap/codex-reviews/g3-organizer-batch/PROCESS-NOTE.md`
        adds a "G3-E3 P0 resolution (2026-05-20)" subsection; P2 capability
        audit row also closed under this commit.
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/docs/dev_log.md` Work Log row records
        P0-Echo and the open-panel TODO; Known Issues row updated.
    
